      "qtype": "mcq",
      "stem": "An ideal gas expands from $2.0\\ \\mathrm{m}^{3}$ to $5.0\\ \\mathrm{m}^{3}$ at a constant pressure of $4.0 \\times 10^{4}\\ \\mathrm{Pa}$. How much work is done by the gas?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$8.0 \\times 10^{4}\\ \\mathrm{J}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$1.2 \\times 10^{5}\\ \\mathrm{J}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$2.0 \\times 10^{5}\\ \\mathrm{J}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$2.8 \\times 10^{5}\\ \\mathrm{J}$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "B",
      "solution": "At constant pressure $W = P\\Delta V = (4.0 \\times 10^{4})(5.0 - 2.0) = 1.2 \\times 10^{5}\\ \\mathrm{J}$.",
